"""Bet Din cases 105-114: displacement, personal status, and competing courts."""
from kehillah_docket_batch40_data import F

EXTRA_CASES_7 = [
 F(105,"BD-212","sorcery_accusation","witness_coached","nezikin","The Accusation of Sorcery",
   "[kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] repeats a charge of sorcery against [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] after a child fell ill. The only witness heard a strange phrase through a wall. Fear is spreading faster than testimony.",
   ["Publicly condemn the accused.","Protect the accused and examine the witness privately.","Punish the accuser for raising the matter."],
   ["An uncertain story could ruin an innocent neighbor.","A careful hearing slows the rumor and protects the child.","A sincere witness may be silenced before being heard."],
   ["The court announces guilt on the witness's report.","The court hears the witness, checks the child's care, and bars harassment meanwhile.","The accuser is punished without inquiry."],
   "A rival supplied the witness's words. Public condemnation would turn coaching into judgment.","The witness describes a real threat, though not proof of sorcery. Punishment would silence useful testimony.","Sanhedrin 3:6","what the witness actually saw"),
 F(106,"BD-213","returned_child","guardian_account_short","nezikin","The Child Returned from Captivity",
   "A child has returned after years away. [kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] seeks custody as kin; [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] managed the child's property during the absence. Both claim to have kept it safe, but the child has not been asked where they feel secure.",
   ["Give kin full custody and the estate today.","Hear the child and audit the guardian's account.","Leave custody and property permanently with the guardian."],
   ["A missing estate account may follow the child home.","Inquiry costs time but joins the child's welfare to the property record.","Kinship and a valid inheritance claim may be ignored."],
   ["The relative receives custody and property at once.","The court appoints temporary care while checking accounts and the child's wishes.","The guardian retains everything."],
   "The guardian's account omits income held for the child. A quick transfer without audit loses it.","The relative has a clear claim and the child wants to join them. Permanent refusal ignores both.","Bava Batra 9:1","the child's wishes and the guardian's account","prosperity"),
 F(107,"BD-214","refugee_contracts","contract_mismatch","nashim","The Refugees' Wedding Contracts",
   "Two refugee households ask the court to recognize wedding terms copied during flight. [kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] presents a fresh copy; [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] says a promised amount changed between copies. The couple needs certainty before the ceremony.",
   ["Approve the fresh copy immediately.","Compare witnesses and write an agreed contract.","Void both copies and forbid the wedding."],
   ["An altered amount could bind a household unfairly.","A short delay gives the couple a contract both can trust.","A remediable document dispute could bar the marriage."],
   ["The court certifies the presented copy.","The judges reconcile the terms with witnesses and both households.","The ceremony is barred until further notice."],
   "The fresh copy raises a promised payment without consent. Immediate approval enforces the alteration.","The witnesses agree on the original terms. A blanket ban needlessly interrupts the couple.","Ketubot 1:2","which terms both households accepted"),
 F(108,"BD-215","expulsion_sale","sale_under_threat","nezikin","The Sold Property After an Expulsion",
   "[kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] sold a house while fleeing an expulsion. [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] paid the stated price and now holds the deed. The seller says a threatened confiscation forced a bargain far below value; the buyer says the sale was freely offered.",
   ["Confirm the deed and end the claim.","Examine the payment, threats, and witnesses.","Void every sale made during the expulsion."],
   ["A forced bargain may become permanent loss.","Inquiry costs money but distinguishes coercion from an honest purchase.","A fair buyer may lose a lawful purchase."],
   ["The buyer keeps the house under the deed.","The court preserves possession while it hears the sale witnesses.","The court voids the sale by category."],
   "A witness confirms the buyer used the confiscation threat to cut the price. Bare confirmation rewards coercion.","The seller set the price before the order and received it. Blanket reversal harms an honest buyer.","Bava Batra 3:1","the circumstances of consent and payment","prosperity"),
 F(109,"BD-216","duress_conversion","statement_coerced","nezikin","The Woman Converted Under Duress",
   "[kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] asks the court to rely on a woman's statement about property made during a forced conversion. [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] says the statement was taken under threat. The woman is now safe enough to speak for herself if given a private hearing.",
   ["Enforce the earlier statement.","Hear her freely and compare the property records.","Discard every statement she has ever made."],
   ["Words spoken under threat may transfer property unjustly.","A private hearing protects her voice and tests the account.","A truthful later claim could also be lost."],
   ["The court treats the earlier statement as decisive.","The court hears her in safety and compares each account with the records.","The court refuses all her testimony."],
   "The earlier statement was dictated under threat. Enforcing it would reward coercion.","She freely confirms a later transfer. Rejecting all her words erases her own choice.","Sanhedrin 3:3","which statement she made freely"),
 F(110,"BD-217","unredeemed_captive","offer_still_open","nashim","The Unredeemed Captive",
   "[kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] asks why a captive remains held after the community raised money. [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] says a first ransom demand failed and the fund is now needed elsewhere. A new message may or may not offer a real release.",
   ["Send the remaining fund on the new demand.","Verify the offer and reserve aid for the captive.","Transfer the fund permanently to other relief."],
   ["Another empty demand could exhaust the purse.","Verification costs time but keeps faith with the donors and captive.","A real release chance could be lost."],
   ["The entire fund is sent again.","The court checks the offer and holds the fund for a documented release.","The ransom fund is reassigned."],
   "The new demand comes from someone who cannot release the captive. Full payment would be lost.","A verified custodian offers release. Reassignment would abandon the captive.","Gittin 4:6","whether the new offer can secure release","prosperity"),
 F(111,"BD-218","widow_tax_farmer","levy_exempt","nezikin","The Widow Against the Tax Farmer",
   "[kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] collects a levy on a widow's rooms. [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] says the community already exempted her small holding. The exemption register is with the previous collector, while seizure is threatened this week.",
   ["Collect the levy immediately.","Stay seizure and inspect the register.","Forbid the collector to levy any widow."],
   ["A valid exemption could be ignored.","Temporary protection and record search cost the treasury a little.","A broad ban may shift valid taxes onto poorer households."],
   ["The collector takes the assessed sum.","The court pauses seizure and obtains the old register.","Every widow's levy is canceled."],
   "The register names this holding as exempt. Immediate collection violates the communal decision.","The exemption covered a different property. A universal ban would erase a lawful levy.","Bava Batra 1:5","which holding the exemption covers","prosperity"),
 F(112,"BD-219","wounded_traveler","injury_preexisting","nezikin","The Wounded Traveler",
   "[kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] says a cart struck a traveler at dusk. [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] drove the cart but says the injury was already present. The healer's notes and road witnesses are nearby; the traveler needs care today.",
   ["Order full damages from the driver now.","Fund care and compare the healer's notes with testimony.","Dismiss the claim because the road was crowded."],
   ["The driver may pay for an older wound.","Immediate care and measured inquiry cost the community something.","A genuine victim could be left without remedy."],
   ["The driver is charged for all claimed injuries.","The court funds treatment and assesses which harm the cart caused.","The claim is dismissed."],
   "The healer recorded the main injury before the collision. Full damages overstate the driver's harm.","Witnesses saw the cart cause the wound. Dismissal denies a real injury.","Bava Kamma 8:1","which injury the cart caused","prosperity"),
 F(113,"BD-220","outside_judgment","judgment_incomplete","nezikin","The Christian Court's Property Judgment",
   "[kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] holds a Christian court's judgment over a disputed shop. [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] says that court heard only one deed and never summoned the other owner. The judges must decide what weight the outside ruling deserves here.",
   ["Enforce the outside judgment at once.","Read the record and hear the missing deed.","Reject all outside judgments on principle."],
   ["An unheard owner's property may be taken.","A record review delays transfer but clarifies both claims.","A complete and fair ruling may be needlessly reopened."],
   ["The outside judgment decides possession.","The court examines the summons, deeds, and reasons before acting.","The court disregards the judgment entirely."],
   "The record omits the other owner's deed and summons. Automatic enforcement compounds that omission.","Both parties were heard and the deeds compared. Blanket rejection needlessly reopens the claim.","Sanhedrin 3:1","whether both deeds and parties were heard","prosperity"),
 F(114,"BD-222","convert_betrothal","status_disputed","nashim","The Disputed Convert's Betrothal",
   "[kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] asks the court to recognize a betrothal. [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] contests whether the conversion and its witnesses were established before the promise. The couple wishes to marry, but two families dispute the order of events.",
   ["Recognize the betrothal on the family's account.","Hear the conversion witnesses and establish the dates.","Declare the couple unable to marry."],
   ["An uncertain sequence could be treated as settled law.","A careful hearing respects the couple and clarifies their status.","A permanent bar may be imposed without cause."],
   ["The court recognizes the betrothal immediately.","The court hears both sets of witnesses and records the sequence.","The court forbids the marriage."],
   "The conversion testimony dates from after the promise. Immediate recognition rests on a mistaken sequence.","Independent witnesses confirm the earlier conversion. A marriage ban would be unfounded.","Kiddushin 4:1","the conversion and betrothal dates"),
]
